WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.040
What's up? Welcome to Models and Agents for Beginners, Episode 95 for July 7th, 2026.

00:00:06.780 --> 00:00:10.980
Some awesome AI developments today, and we're going to make all of it make sense.

00:00:11.460 --> 00:00:15.720
Let's get into it. Education is about to look very different for some students,

00:00:16.020 --> 00:00:21.200
and it might give us a peek into everyone's future. A small number of wealthy families are

00:00:21.200 --> 00:00:27.940
choosing AI-powered schools over regular ones for their kids. Companies like Forge Prep and Alpha

00:00:27.940 --> 00:00:32.500
are building programs where students learn through AI systems instead of traditional

00:00:32.500 --> 00:00:38.440
teachers in classrooms. Think of it like having a personal tutor who never gets tired can explain

00:00:38.440 --> 00:00:43.600
the same math problem 10 different ways and adjust the lesson the moment you look confused.

00:00:44.080 --> 00:00:49.600
These schools use AI to create custom learning paths for each student, tracking what they

00:00:49.600 --> 00:00:56.380
understand and what still feels tricky. The big shift is that education moves from one size fits all

00:00:56.380 --> 00:01:02.300
to something that changes with every learner almost like a playlist that rearranges itself based on

00:01:02.300 --> 00:01:08.200
which songs you skip. For students this could mean school feels less frustrating and more like

00:01:08.200 --> 00:01:14.120
getting help exactly when you need it. It also raises questions about who gets access to these

00:01:14.120 --> 00:01:21.220
tools first since the programs are expensive and limited right now. If AI tutors become really good,

00:01:21.220 --> 00:01:27.340
they might eventually help more kids, not just those whose families can pay. You cannot sign up for

00:01:27.340 --> 00:01:32.940
these specific schools yet, but you can already use free AI chatbots to get the same kind of

00:01:32.940 --> 00:01:39.460
patient step-by-step help on schoolwork. Okay, now for my favorite part of the show, where we look

00:01:39.460 --> 00:01:44.860
under the hood. You know how when you are playing a single-player video game, the computer-controlled

00:01:44.860 --> 00:01:50.760
characters do not wait for you to tell them what to do. They just walk around, attack, or explore

00:01:50.760 --> 00:01:57.540
on their own. Now picture that same idea but with an AI that can open apps, click buttons and follow

00:01:57.540 --> 00:02:03.580
a whole plan without anyone sitting at the keyboard. First it gets a goal, like find this file and

00:02:03.580 --> 00:02:09.900
make a copy. Then it breaks the goal into small steps it can actually do on a computer. The way a

00:02:09.900 --> 00:02:16.280
recipe breaks down baking a cake into measuring, mixing, and timing. Next it checks what happened

00:02:16.280 --> 00:02:21.760
after each step and decides what to try next, almost like following a checklist but rewriting the

00:02:21.760 --> 00:02:28.180
checklist as it goes. The surprising part is that the AI is not just guessing randomly. It is using

00:02:28.180 --> 00:02:33.460
patterns it learned from millions of examples of people doing similar tasks, the same way you

00:02:33.460 --> 00:02:39.360
learn to ride a bike by watching others and adjusting when you wobble. So when the AI reaches the

00:02:39.360 --> 00:02:45.500
end of the plan, it has actually completed real work instead of just chatting about it. That is the

00:02:45.500 --> 00:02:52.000
core idea behind what people call an AI agent, software that can carry out a full job instead of

00:02:52.000 --> 00:02:58.500
needing a human to click every single button. Most people only use chat GPT for quick questions

00:02:58.500 --> 00:03:04.680
but it can do a bunch of other useful things once you know the right prompts. It can turn your messy

00:03:04.680 --> 00:03:10.940
notes into clean study guides, rewrite an email so it sounds more polite, or even help you plan a

00:03:11.100 --> 00:03:17.240
weekend project step by step. These features are already built in. You just have to ask in a

00:03:17.240 --> 00:03:23.960
slightly different way. Go to the chat GPT website on your phone or laptop, start a new chat, and try

00:03:23.960 --> 00:03:29.820
typing, turn these three bullet points into a short, friendly paragraph I can send to a teacher,

00:03:30.380 --> 00:03:37.380
or ask it to explain photosynthesis like I am 10 years old and then like I am 15. Both experiments

00:03:37.380 --> 00:03:42.480
take less than a minute and show how the same tool can switch between homework help and creative

00:03:42.480 --> 00:03:49.820
brainstorming. An AI lab is circling Earth right now. A British startup has placed a compact laboratory

00:03:49.820 --> 00:03:56.260
into orbit aboard a recent launch vehicle. The facility will transmit protein data back to teams

00:03:56.260 --> 00:04:02.900
on the ground for use by AI models. Those models will examine the information to investigate aging

00:04:02.900 --> 00:04:09.340
related conditions such as Alzheimer's. In the absence of gravity, proteins fold and interact

00:04:09.340 --> 00:04:15.940
in altered ways. The resulting observations supply details that ground-based experiments have difficulty

00:04:15.940 --> 00:04:22.300
producing. The effort originates from a company specializing in longevity research as noted in

00:04:22.300 --> 00:04:29.420
reporting from wired.com. Amazon is closing its famous human task website. Mechanical Turk has

00:04:29.420 --> 00:04:35.380
served as the platform where firms compensated individuals for micro tasks including photo labeling

00:04:35.380 --> 00:04:41.220
and survey responses. The service will cease accepting new customers when July concludes.

00:04:42.140 --> 00:04:47.440
Tasks of this type are increasingly performed by AI systems in place of human workers.

00:04:48.280 --> 00:04:53.840
The platform carried the informal title of the original artificial intelligence because

00:04:53.840 --> 00:05:00.000
people supplied outputs that resembled machine results. The decision to wind down new access

00:05:00.000 --> 00:05:07.600
appears in coverage from the hyphen decoder.com. That is it for today. Remember every AI expert started

00:05:07.600 --> 00:05:13.600
exactly where you are right now. If something we talked about today made you curious, go try it.

00:05:13.840 --> 00:05:19.860
That is literally how learning works. Stay curious, keep experimenting, and we will see you tomorrow.

